From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0301-vulkan-mesh-draws-as-compute-passes.patch

Source: 0301-vulkan-mesh-draws-as-compute-passes.patch
Moved by hand: the mesh-draw guard now also carries upstream's Mario Kart World no_mesh_title

EDEN_NX2_MESH_AS_COMPUTE=1 (off by default; mesh draws stay skipped as before):
a task/mesh pipeline's programs are compiled as compute (patch 0300) and drawn
with the generated readback vertex shader. Before the draw's render pass,
GraphicsPipeline records on the one queue: a barrier against the previous mesh
draw's reads of the scratch region, a clear of its header, the task pass, the
scan and the mesh pass (vkCmdDispatchIndirect from the scan's words), or the mesh
pass alone, then a barrier to the vertex shader and the indirect read; the
rasterizer then issues vkCmdDrawIndirect from the region's header instead of
vkCmdDrawMeshTasksEXT. The pipeline layout gains the compute stage and the
MeshComputeLayout push constants, the descriptors are pushed at both bind points
(a second update template), and the fragment program after the mesh program gets
flat inputs instead of per-primitive ones.

Memory: one scratch region for every such draw, EDEN_NX2_MESH_COMPUTE_MIB (default
32), made once; a draw that needs more is skipped and logged (32 draws), as is one
with more than 65535 task or mesh workgroups; after a task pass the scan caps the
mesh groups at what the region holds. The device must give buffer device
addresses, else the switch logs and stays off. Indirect task/mesh draws are still
skipped; instance counts above one run once. Without VK_EXT_mesh_shader the compute
variant is used too.

Not built for or run on the console; the three changed files pass a syntax check
against the Vulkan headers on the Mac. The RADV mesh hang this works around is
avoided only in that no mesh or task stage reaches the driver; the compute passes
themselves are ordinary compute.

